<GuideLayout
  title="Privacy policy of this Canadian salary calculator 2026"
  description="How Canada Net Pay handles your data. No personal salary or financial data is collected, stored, or transmitted. All calculations run in your browser."
  publishDate="2026-06-27"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy Policy' }]}
>
  <p><em>Last updated: October 2, 2026</em></p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>
    Canada Net Pay is a static website. All calculations run entirely in your browser.
    We do not collect, store, or transmit any salary or personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Collection</h2>
  <p><strong>The calculator collects nothing.</strong> Specifically:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>No salary, income, or financial information is sent to any server.</li>
    <li>No account registration is required.</li>
    <li>No advertising cookies are used.</li>
    <li>No personal information is sold to third parties.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How the Calculator Works</h2>
  <p>All tax calculations are performed client-side in your web browser using JavaScript. The numbers you enter never leave your device. When you share a URL with calculator parameters (e.g., salary amount and province), that information is encoded in the URL hash fragment, which is not sent to our servers. If someone opens such a link, the page address, including those parameters, is part of what our audience measurement records (see below).</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>We use Microsoft Clarity to see how pages are used. It records clicks, scrolling, pages viewed and their address, device and browser type, and an approximate location derived from the IP address. What you type into a field is masked in your browser and is not sent. Microsoft Clarity sets the cookies <code>_clck</code> (one year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day), and Microsoft may set <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains.</p>
  <p>A notice tells you about it on your first visit. Clarity runs unless you choose “Opt out”; once you do, it is no longer loaded and its cookies are removed. You can change your choice at any time through the “Cookie settings” link at the bottom of every page. Session recordings are kept for 30 days and aggregated data for up to 13 months. Microsoft may process this data outside Canada, including in the United States; its handling is described in its <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">privacy statement</a>.</p>

  <h2>Local Storage</h2>
  <p>The website uses your browser’s local storage to save your theme preference (light/dark mode) and your choice about audience measurement (key <code>consent-choice</code>). This data stays on your device and is not transmitted anywhere.</p>

  <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>The website is hosted on static hosting infrastructure. Apart from Microsoft Clarity, described above, we do not use third-party advertising, tracking pixels, or social media widgets that could collect your data.</p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this page
    with an updated date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this privacy policy, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
  </p>
